  "body": "A ball nose's corner radius is its ball, half the diameter. The tool editor now says so and stops offering a field that does nothing.\n\n### What was wrong\n\n- On a ball nose, every part of the code that cuts or checks already uses half the diameter as the corner, whatever the `corner_r` field holds: `Cutter::of` sets the corner to the radius, `Tool::profile` draws the full dome, and the stock sim sweeps the exact sphere.\n- The tool editor still showed an editable \"Corner radius\" on a ball nose. Typing in it changed nothing that is cut, which is what the reporter saw.\n- A draft retyped from an end mill saved a ball nose with `corner_r = 0`, and the library summary then read `corner r 0.00`.\n\n### What changed\n\n- `Tool::tip_corner_r` (tools crate) states the rule in one place: a ball nose's (or probe's) corner is `d / 2`; every other kind answers its own field.\n- The editor shows a ball nose's corner as text (`3.000 mm` for a 6 mm ball, \"half the diameter - a ball nose's whole tip is its ball\") with no field to edit. Every other kind is unchanged, so the bull nose still edits its corner.\n- `ToolUi::to_tool` saves a ball nose with `corner_r = d / 2`, so the document holds the radius that is cut. The kind mapping moved into `ToolUi::tool_kind` so the editor can name kinds instead of numbering them.\n- The tool library summary reads `tip_corner_r`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/263-ball-corner.md`. It says why the field is not also hidden on the kinds that never read it (end mill, drill, lathe kinds): that changes the end-mill editor's pixel golden, which needs regenerating on the CI platform (#255).\n\n### Tests\n\n- `tools::tests::a_ball_noses_corner_is_half_its_diameter_whatever_the_field_holds`\n- `egui_app::ball_corner_tests` (new file, egui_kittest over the real editor window and library page):\n  - `a_ball_noses_corner_is_shown_as_its_ball_with_no_field_to_edit`\n  - `applying_a_ball_nose_saves_its_corner_as_half_the_diameter`\n  - `the_library_summary_reads_a_ball_noses_corner_as_its_ball`\n  - `a_bull_nose_keeps_its_corner_field` (guards the other side)\n\nWith `state.rs` and `pages.rs` put back to `main`, the three ball-nose UI tests fail and the bull-nose one passes.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 0015347 plus this branch)\n\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick`: the tools lib and the ui lib plus 10 ui suites. Everything passes except the three UI pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`), which fail the same way on clean `main` on this machine. `tool_editor_snapshot` (an end mill) is off by 2080 pixels both on `main` and on this branch, so the end-mill editor picture is unchanged.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- I did not open the windowed app by hand; the editor checks are the kittest tests above, which draw the real window code. Not run on Linux or macOS.\n\nChangelog: A ball nose's corner radius shows as half its diameter in the tool editor, read-only, and is saved that way (#263)\n\nFixes #263\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
